{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792336985,"nonce":"Nro/4R5s4RJWQTQjzGv43Dz3zsU=","title":"Fibers have no time budget, and cancelling one does not stop it mid-run","message":"FiberCfg has no deadline; should_yield_early appears only in comments (hir.rs:997, fiber_backend.rs:122), so krio-fiber's set_deadline_ms cannot be reached and a fiber that never yields blocks the host thread. Cancel sets a flag seen at the next resume, which returns Done without running the body (krio_adapter fiber.rs:303); programs have no is_cancelled symbol (zrtl.rs:2336-2371). A host stepping scripts once per UI frame needs a budget it can slice by, for example an epoch word bumped by a timer and checked at loop back-edges, calling a poll helper only when it changed (the pattern Ash uses); the Cranelift back-edge probes serve OSR only.\n\nReported from RayDE's RayScript planning (RayDE git-bug 971d58e, latest comment); claims marked verified were checked in the code at 5c58f753, the rest come from a read-only review and their line numbers may drift.","files":null}]}